    "conventions": "Input IPA must be NFC. Diphthongs must carry U+032F COMBINING INVERTED BREVE BELOW on the off-glide (aɪ̯), otherwise two consecutive vowel symbols read as hiatus. Consonant gemination may be written doubled (tt) or with U+02D0 (tː); both map to espeak length/doubling. Long vowels use U+02D0 (aː).",
    "openReviewItems": [
      "r-sounds: espeak la renders single r as R (trill); its own dictionary renders geminate rr as r+ɾ. Choose our convention (rr → RR, or Rr, or rɾ→Rr).",
      "Short-vowel quality: espeak la realizes short i/u/e/o as lax [ɪ ʊ ɛ ɔ] (Allen, Vox Latina). Table accepts both tense and lax IPA symbols for the same targets; G2P notation decision pending.",
      "ui diphthong (cui/huic) not covered — needs academic decision ([kuj]? [kʊɪ̯]?).",
      "Aspiration: ph_latin defines <h> as ipa ʰ modifier for ph/th/ch in Greek loanwords — include or simplify to p/t/k + h?"
    ]
  },
